Package: spark-video-processor
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Devin Block <devin@devinblock.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: video
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/moocowsheep/SparkVideoProcessor
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: python3, avahi-daemon
Description: Real-time ST 2110 video processor on NVIDIA Blackwell GPUs
 DPDK-based SMPTE ST 2110-20/-30 receive/transmit with hardware-paced TX,
 PTP (ST 2059-2) genlock, fixed end-to-end latency with an ST 2110-30 audio
 relay, Blackmagic IP10 (10:8) codec for 2160p59.94/60 over 10G, optical-flow
 2x frame-rate conversion, and a CUDA filter chain (AI super-resolution,
 scaling, sharpen, proc-amp, noise reduction, film grain).
 .
 Ships the engine (st2110_pipeline), the control daemon with web dashboard
 (spark_controld, systemd unit spark-video-processor.service) and an NMOS
 IS-04/IS-05 node (spark_nmos_node, unit spark-nmos-node.service).
 .
 Requires the NVIDIA driver (libcuda, libnvidia-opticalflow) and a Blackwell
 GPU with an optical-flow engine: DGX Spark / GB10 (arm64) and RTX PRO 6000
 Blackwell / GB20x (amd64) are the validated targets. Hardware-paced TX
 additionally needs a ConnectX NIC with REAL_TIME_CLOCK_ENABLE=1; without it
 the pipeline still runs, unpaced. CUDA runtime libraries (cudart, NPP) are
 bundled under /usr/lib/spark-video-processor/lib.
